<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morphou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Güzelyurt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morphou is a town in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, near the bay of the same name, in a fertile plain known for citrus growing. The ancient city-kingdom of Soloi lay on the bay to the west, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skouriotissa">Skouriotissa</a>. Since 1974 the town has been under Turkish Cypriot control, under the name Güzelyurt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morphou.jpg" alt="Morphou" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seksen iki yüz kırk beş · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morphou_orange_monument.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
